<title>USA: Carnegie Bancorp to convert warrants.</title>
<headline>Carnegie Bancorp to convert warrants.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carnegie Bancorp said on Thursday that it retained investment banking firms Janney Montgomery Scott and First Colonial Securities Group to help exercise its outstanding common stock purchase warrants.</p>
<p>The warrants, which expire on August 18, allow holders to purchase 1.157 Carnegie shares for $15.09, an effective price of $13.04 per share, the company said in a news release.</p>
<p>Carnegie shares closed Wednesday at 17-9/16.</p>
